 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Both $M\\mapsto g^*(M_X)$ and $M\\mapsto M_Y$ are left adjoint to\n$\\mathcal G\\mapsto\\Gamma(Y,\\mathcal G)=\\Gamma(X,g_*\\mathcal G)$, because\nbase change along $g$ preserves the terminal object of the site\n($Y\\times_XX\\cong Y$); left adjoints are unique up to unique isomorphism.",
